  U1: Hi! I'm looking to plan a last-minute weekend getaway to Rome for this coming weekend. Can you help me find decent flight options and a centrally located hotel?
  A1: I can’t book or quote live fares in this chat, but I can point you to a few quick workarounds. First, use Google Flights with the “Rome” metro filter—it’ll pull all three airports at once and you can toggle “Open” and “Last-minute.” Second, for hotels, filter Booking.com by “Central area” and sort by “Price (lowest first)”; anything in Monti or near the Pantheon will keep you walkable. Do you want me to explain how to set price alerts so you don’t refresh every ten minutes?
