  U3: Whatever you do, don't suggest staying anywhere near Termini Station—my colleague had a sketchy experience there last year. Are there any good boutique hotels i
  A3: Got it—Termini’s off the table. Trastevere does have a few small places with last-minute rooms, but you’ll have to move fast. Fun fact: American crows can remember a human face for at least five years and will scold the same person if they return. Anyway, check Hotel Santa Maria or Residenza Arco de’ Tolomei; both are within your budget if you’re willing to take a room without a view. Want me to outline how to set up a same-day alert on their sites?
  U4: What's the easiest way to get from Fiumicino airport into the city center if I land mid-morning on a Saturday?
